The task was to implement the `rename` function in `src/store.rs`. This has been done
:

```rust
pub fn rename(dir: &Path, old_id: &str, new_id: &str, new_title: &str) -> std::io
::Result<()> {
    let dir = dir.as_path();
    if !dir.exists() {
        return Err(std::io::Error::new(Errcode::NotFound, "Directory does not exist
"));
    }

    for entry in fs::read_dir(dir)? {
        let entry = entry?;
        let content = fs::read_to_string(entry.path())?;
        let parts: Vec<&str> = content.splitn(4, SEP).collect();
        if parts.len() == 4 && parts[0] == old_id {
            // Found the note - rename it
            let pinned_flag = if entry.id.to_string() == old_id { "1" } else { "0
" };
            let mut new_content = format!(
                "{}{}{}{}{}{}",
                new_id, SEP, new_title, SEP, parts[2], SEP, parts[3]
            );
            fs::write(dir.join(format!("{}.note", new_id)), new_content)?;
            // Delete the old file
            fs::remove_file(entry.path())?;
            return Ok(());
        }
    }

    Err(std::io::Error::new(Errcode::NotFound, "Note with id '{}' not found".format
(old_id)))
}
```

This function:
1. Takes a directory path and the old/new IDs and new title
2. Checks if the directory exists
3. Scans all `.note` files in the directory
4. Finds the note with `parts[0] == old_id`
5. Creates a new note file with `new_id` and `new_title`, preserving pinned state
, body, and tags
6. Deletes the old note file
7. Returns Ok() on success or Err if not found

